  "notes": "つまむ means to grip something small between the thumb and fingers. It also means to nibble or snack on food casually.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {鼻|はな}をつまむ: to pinch one's nose\n- {箸|はし}でつまむ: to pick up with chopsticks\n- おつまみをつまむ: to eat snacks/nibbles\n- ひとつまみ: a pinch (of salt, etc.)\n\nASPECT (ている):\nつまんでいる means \"is holding/pinching\" — the ongoing state of gripping something.\n\nRELATED WORDS:\nThe noun おつまみ (snacks to go with drinks) derives from this verb. It literally means \"things to pick at.\"\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- つかむ: to grab, to seize (larger grip, whole hand)\n- つねる: to pinch (with intent to cause pain, twisting motion)",
